12287	{"artifactId":"LLD-b2687832a8c75877-s1","entry":{"id":"migrated-LLD-b2687832a8c75877-s1-review","actor":{"id":"insrc:daemon","kind":"agent","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-09T16:36:55.060Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"fix-targets-defect.1","ref":"fix-targets-defect","item":"fix-targets-defect","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The LLD delivers every point of the ISSUE's fix intent, including 'narrow-pane count chips with folded empty stages' (Mock E).","evidence":"ISSUE fix intent: 'narrow-pane count chips with folded empty stages'; Mock E expects 'count chips, and empty stages folded into \"Other stages · 0 matching\"'. The LLD replaces the fold with 'empty stage labels wrap onto one compact line' (BOARD_STYLE postcondition; Open question 2). Nothing in the LLD says non-empty stage headings get a count chip. Today board-host.ts:146 renders the heading as plain text, make('h2',col.label+' ('+col.total+')'). The only BOARD_WEBVIEW_SCRIPT postcondition on counts is for empty sections ('label and 0'). Most of the fix intent is covered (app bar, tone pills, compact id plus task count, six columns, rollup rows, details chain with 'Not recorded', conflict box, four panels). This one item is changed (no fold) and partly left unspecified (count chips on non-empty groups). [files: docs/standalone/defect-against-epic-e2-6a131558-vs-E20261009b2687832/ISSUE.md, vscode-plugin/src/delivery/board-host.ts]","action":"Either get the fold deviation confirmed as a deliberate change to the fix intent, or deliver a fold that does not hide content (for example a disclosure that is open by default). In both cases, state in the script postconditions that every narrow-pane stage heading renders its count as a chip, and add a test for it.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Today StatusView carries only message/partialNotice, the empty, failed and partial states go to single #status, #notice and #empty lines, #details is an <aside> after #board, and the Epics tab renders EpicGroupView stage groups of cards through renderGroup.","evidence":"board-protocol.ts:27-33 StatusView {state, takenAt, message, partialNotice, stale}. board-host.ts:269-271 renders `<p id=\"empty\"></p><div id=\"board\" class=\"board\"></div><aside id=\"details\" ... hidden></aside>`. board-host.ts:257 renders `<p id=\"notice\"></p>`. board-host.ts:119-128 has renderGroup over m.epics and m.notInEpic. board-views.ts:29-46 groupOf builds the StageGroupView[] of cards. CardView (board-protocol.ts:50-60) has no compact id and no task summary. The LLD's description of today's code is accurate. [files: vscode-plugin/src/delivery/board-state.ts, vscode-plugin/src/delivery/board-host.ts, vscode-plugin/src/delivery/board-protocol.ts, vscode-plugin/src/delivery/board-views.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The new values can be derived from fields the plugin already reads: item.stage.route for the route-aware chain, validation for taskSummary, tasks for taskCount, and evidence kinds.","evidence":"delivery-contract.ts:59-61 DeliveryItemView picks 'stage', 'evidence', 'tasks', 'validation', 'storyLevelResult' and 'conflict'. types.ts:294 has stage: { stage; route: DeliveryRoute; reason }. types.ts:157 DeliveryRoute = 'full-chain' | 'feature' | 'small' | 'small-bugfix' | 'sized-bugfix' | 'trivial' | 'unknown'. types.ts:214 validation has {passed, failed, unrecorded, unplanned}. No change to the daemon contract is needed. [files: vscode-plugin/src/delivery/delivery-contract.ts, src/workflow/delivery/types.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The listed change sites for threading `now` into statusView are complete: createDeliveryBoardHost only 'passes deps.now() into boardDownMessages'.","evidence":"statusView has a second caller that the LLD does not name: board-host.ts:413 announceRefresh, `const message = statusView(state.status).message;`. The new signature statusView(status, now) makes that call fail the typecheck. The existing tests board-state.test.ts:29 and :36 also call boardDownMessages(state, DISPLAY_LABELS, {}) with three arguments. The 2.10 postcondition names only the boardDownMessages call path. [files: vscode-plugin/src/delivery/board-host.ts, vscode-plugin/src/delivery/board-state.ts]","action":"Add announceRefresh's statusView call (board-host.ts:413) and the existing board-state.test.ts call sites to the change list. Alternatively make `now` optional, with freshnessLabel null when it is omitted.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"preserved-behaviour.1","ref":"preserved-behaviour","item":"preserved-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The AC-09 invariant is real and survives the rollup rewrite: board, rollup and issue views all derive from selectMatches, and every match falls into exactly one rollup group, so the row totals sum to the board's totals.items.","evidence":"board-views.ts:61-72 calls selectMatches and routes each match either to notInEpic (standalone or epic === null) or to byEpic. board-model.ts:240-248 builds the board totals.items from the same selectMatches. The LLD keeps buildEpicRollup's listing rule ('unnarrowed' at board-views.ts:49-51) and only changes groupOf's output shape, so the partition is unchanged. [files: vscode-plugin/src/delivery/board-views.ts, vscode-plugin/src/delivery/board-model.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"preserved-behaviour.2","ref":"preserved-behaviour","item":"preserved-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The new route-aware chain cannot break the details view or refresh on published data: ChainRowView.kind is 'DEF'|'HLD'|'ISSUE'|'LLD'|'PLAN'|'BUILD', yet the chain lists 'every kind actually recorded', and the error-path table expects a throw on 'an evidence kind the plugin does not know'.","evidence":"types.ts:23 DeliveryArtifactKind = 'SPEC' | 'DEF' | 'HLD' | 'LLD' | 'PLAN' | 'BUILD' | 'CR' | 'ISSUE' | 'EXT' | 'AMD'. Items routinely carry CR evidence (fixtures CR-dfc0371b7200f5b5-s1) and SPEC/EXT/AMD records. Those are published kinds, not malformed data. The LLD never says whether the chain drops them. If the 'every kind actually recorded' postcondition is followed, or the error path's throw is taken, any reviewed story's details would fail. board-host.ts:317-321 builds detailsMessage inside apply(), and refresh() at 366-380 turns a throw there into a failed refresh over the previous board. That breaks the promise that the board renders all published data. [files: src/workflow/delivery/types.ts, vscode-plugin/src/delivery/board-host.ts]","action":"State explicitly that the chain shows only the six chain kinds and ignores SPEC, CR, EXT and AMD evidence, which stays in Records. Remove 'unknown evidence kind' from the throw cases. Add a test that a story with CR and SPEC evidence gets a chain without those kinds and no error.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The unit fixtures pin the compactId rule against the real canonical id format ('E20261009abcdef01-S001').","evidence":"types.ts:83: 'Canonical work-item id (\"E<date><hash8>[:S<nnn>][:T<nnn>]\"); an H-form or \":R(<raw>)\" fallback'. graph.ts:299 mints `H${hash}:S${pad(ordinal)}`. The separator is ':', not '-'. If the fixture and the ac1 test use '-S001', a compactId parser written to pass them would fall back to the full id for every real story card. The test would pass while the board shows the wrong thing. H-form ids also carry ':S<nnn>' with a hash, so whether they count as 'no 8-hex hash' needs pinning. [files: src/workflow/delivery/types.ts, src/workflow/delivery/graph.ts]","action":"Change the fixture to 'E20261009abcdef01:S001' and spell the parse rule out against types.ts:83. Add cases for task ids (':T<nnn>'), H-form ids ('H<hash>:S001') and ':R(<raw>)' fallback ids.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"tests.2","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The new acceptance tests would fail without the fix. Example: ac6 expects parseBoardUpMessage to accept {type:'clear-filters'}, and ac2 expects rollup rows carrying taskCount and attentionCount.","evidence":"board-protocol.ts:222-253: the parser switch has no 'clear-filters' case, so the default returns null. board-views.ts:36-45: EpicGroupView has no taskCount, attentionCount or attentionLabel. ItemDetailsViewModel.conflict is a string today (board-protocol.ts:172), and the existing test asserts a string at board-details.test.ts:102. So the ac2, ac3, ac4 and ac6 unit tests fail on today's code. One inconsistency: the ac6 'rejects it with extra fields' check introduces strictness that no other up-message has, since the existing cases ignore extra fields. It is deliberate and testable, but not required by the fix. [files: vscode-plugin/src/delivery/board-protocol.ts, vscode-plugin/src/delivery/board-views.ts]","action":"Optional: either drop the 'rejects extra fields' assertion to match how the other up-messages are parsed, or note in the LLD that clear-filters is deliberately stricter than the rest.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":4,"low":4,"unverified":0},"template":"design-issue","reviewedAt":"2026-10-09T16:36:55.060Z","model":"cli-claude:opus","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{"change-sites.2":{"findingId":"change-sites.2","status":"resolved","note":"Applied. statusView's preconditions now name both callers: boardDownMessages and the host's announceRefresh (board-host.ts:413). createDeliveryBoardHost's returns passes deps.now() into both. Migration step 4 also covers updating the existing three-argument boardDownMessages calls in board-state.test.ts and the other tests, and board-state.test.ts joins StatusView's call sites.","resolvedAt":"2026-10-09T16:41:08.047Z"},"preserved-behaviour.2":{"findingId":"preserved-behaviour.2","status":"resolved","note":"Applied. The ChainRowView data model and buildItemDetails' postconditions now state that only DEF, HLD, ISSUE, LLD, PLAN and BUILD become chain rows. Evidence of the other published kinds (SPEC, CR, EXT, AMD) is skipped by the chain and stays under Records, so it can never throw. The 'unknown evidence kind' example is removed from the error cases. A new edge case and an ac3 test cover a story with CR, SPEC, EXT and AMD evidence getting a chain without them and no error.","resolvedAt":"2026-10-09T16:41:08.048Z"},"tests.1":{"findingId":"tests.1","status":"resolved","note":"Applied. The compactId rule is now spelled out against types.ts:83 (\"E<date><hash8>[:S<nnn>][:T<nnn>]\", H-form, ':R(<raw>)'), with worked examples. The fixtures use 'E20261009abcdef01:S001', the epic-level 'E20261009abcdef01', the H-form 'Habcdef0123456789:S002' and a ':R(<raw>)' id. The ac1 test asserts each case. ':T<nnn>' is noted as never reaching a card, because cards are stories and issues.","resolvedAt":"2026-10-09T16:41:08.049Z"},"fix-targets-defect.1":{"findingId":"fix-targets-defect.1","status":"resolved","note":"Deviation confirmed by the user (2026-10-09). Narrow panes list the non-empty stage groups first, then wrap the empty stage labels, each with its 0 count chip, onto one compact line. There is no 'Other stages · 0 matching' disclosure, because the same DOM serves the wide board, where the PRD keeps empty columns visible, and S005's no-hiding rule forbids collapsing them. Applied: the BOARD_WEBVIEW_SCRIPT postconditions now require every stage heading (wide and narrow) to render its total as a count chip, and ac5 gains a test for it.","resolvedAt":"2026-10-09T16:42:47.219Z"}}}}}}
